;; expect: main.run runnable no_l_identity
;; §8.4 slice 3.28 rule 3's last sentence: an E-first body that takes an instance builds it as a
;; program with no generated definition. `run` is E-first through `tag`, a fn over a Symbol (E
;; only — the symbol it passes has no L form, `no_l_identity`), and takes the template `mapi` at
;; the named fn `digit`: INSTANCE main.main_mapi.of.main_digit_0 … equations= (none), RUNNABLE fn
;; main.run why=no_l_identity route=e_first (kernel/test/template_test.sh reads both).
;; Until slice 4.3 landing 1 the fixture was examples/template/template_main.shard's main, E-first
;; for its extern's sake; the extern an opaque constant in L now, that main is typed and its
;; instance has its equations
(import Init Int.decEq)
(fn mapi ((f (-> Int Int)) (xs (List Int))) (List Int) (measure (struct xs))
  (match xs
    (List.nil List.nil)
    ((List.cons x t) (List.cons (f x) (mapi f t)))))
(fn digit ((n Int)) Int (+ 48 n))
(fn tag ((s Symbol)) Nat 0)
(fn run ((xs (List Int))) (List Int) (match (tag (quote x)) (_ (mapi digit xs))))
